From d011b052b8d8c0b9ba4c3298e92e5e03bbfbd6b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Travis Gilbert <1travisgilbert@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 02:43:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(input): take platform selections with their direction
 and report UTF-16 length

InputBaseState implemented selected_text_range but not its setters, so a
browser editing island could not hand a selection back. It now
implements set_text_selection (range plus direction; a caret is never
reversed), set_selected_text_range (forward), and text_length_utf16, the
whole document's length in UTF-16 units that a whole-document conduit
mirrors. Ranges are clipped and expanded to character boundaries like
set_selected_range.

Moves the Zed pin to 1c7e4989 (the editing island patch), which adds the
set_text_selection platform hook.
